ProjectScale: SDD

Purpose:
  Define project scale levels L0-L5. Scale is one of the primary inputs
  to architecture selection.

Owns: architecture\levels.sdd
Levels:

  L0:
    name: Prototype
    users: < 100
    team: 1
    availability: none
    architecture: single app

  L1:
    name: Small
    users: 100 - 1K
    team: 1-3
    availability: 99%
    architecture: modular application, single DB

  L2:
    name: Production
    users: 1K - 100K
    team: 3-10
    availability: 99.9%
    architecture: modular architecture, observability, backup

  L3:
    name: Large
    users: 100K - 1M
    team: 10-50
    availability: 99.95%
    architecture: distributed components, advanced caching, queues

  L4:
    name: Critical
    users: 1M - 10M
    team: 50-200
    availability: 99.99%
    architecture: HA multi-zone, disaster recovery, advanced observability

  L5:
    name: Massive
    users: 10M+
    team: 200+
    availability: 99.999%
    architecture: multi-region, extreme scale, strict compliance

Selection:
  AI MUST calculate ProjectScale from:
    DAU/MAU, RPS, Peak RPS, Concurrent users
    Data volume, Read/write ratio, Latency requirements
    Availability requirements, Team size, Budget, Compliance requirements

  ProjectScale is distinct from:
    SecurityLevel (security/levels.sdd)
    TestLevel (testing/levels.sdd)
    ArchitecturePattern (patterns.sdd)

Navigation:
  Patterns: @patterns.sdd
  Availability: @availability.sdd

State: +
